<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cenbank bond rate slips to 2.5844 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cenbank bond rate slips to 2.5844 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's benchmark overnight rate dropped to 2.5844 percent a month, from 2.6149 percent last week, at today's 7.0 billion real sale of 56-day Central Bank Bonds (BBC), dealers said.</p>
<p>The auction's result was in line with market expectations, they added.</p>
<p>The 56-day bonds will mature on January 8. Today's auction is expected to add 719 million reais to the banking system, with 7.5 billion reais in old bonds coming due Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415</p>
